ld be on line A1C1? No, D is on the radical axis y=-2x. Let me check if D is on A1C1. A1C1: (5-33t, 56t). For D=(-1/2, 1): 56t = 1 → t = 1/56. 5 - 33/56 = (280-33)/56 = 247/56 ≠ -1/2. So D is not on A1C1.\n\nSo X, D, Y are not collinear in general. Then XD/DY is the ratio of distances? Or is it a directed ratio on a line?\n\nHmm, the problem says \"Calculate the value of XD/DY\". If X, D, Y are not collinear, this would be a ratio of lengths (distances). But that seems unusual for a geometry problem. Let me reconsider.\n\nWait, maybe I have the wrong D. Let me reconsider the problem. D is the second intersection of circumcircles of ABC and A1BC1. I found D = (-1/2, 1). Let me verify D is on circumcircle of A1BC1: x²+y²-5x-15/4 y = 1/4 + 1 + 5/2 - 15/4 = 1/4 + 1 + 10/4 - 15/4 = (1+4+10-15)/4 = 0. ✓. And on circumcircle of ABC: x²+y²-14x-33/4 y = 1/4+1+7-33/4 = 1/4+1+7-33/4 = (1+4+28-33)/4 = 0. ✓.\n\nSo D = (-1/2, 1) is correct.\n\nNow X, D, Y: X=(-389/338, 1764/169), D=(-1/2, 1), Y=(209/22, -84/11).\n\nLet me check if they're collinear. \nX = (-389/338, 3528/338), D = (-169/338, 338/338), Y = (209/22, -168/22).\n\nVector DX = X - D = (-389/338 + 1/2, 1764/169 - 1) = (-389/338 + 169/338, (1764-169)/169) = (-220/338, 1595/169) = (-110/169, 1595/169).\nVector DY = Y - D = (209/22 + 1/2, -84/11 - 1) = (209/22 + 11/22, (-84-11)/11) = (220/22, -95/11) = (10, -95/11).\n\nDX = (-110/169, 1595/169) = (1/169)(-110, 1595).\nDY = (10, -95/11) = (1/11)(110, -95).\n\nDX direction: (-110, 1595) = -5(22, -319).\nDY direction: (110, -95) = 5(22, -19).\n\nThese are not parallel (22/-319 ≠ 22/-19). So X, D, Y are not collinear. So XD/DY is the ratio of distances.\n\nLet me compute |DX| and |DY|.\n\n|DX|² = (110/169)² + (1595/169)² = (110² + 1595²)/169² = (12100 + 2544025)/28561 = 2556125/28561.\n|DY|² = 10² + (95/11)² = 100 + 9025/121 = (12100 + 9025)/121 = 21125/121.\n\nXD/DY = sqrt(2556125/28561) / sqrt(21125/121) = sqrt(2556125/28561 · 121/21125).\n\n2556125/21125 = ? 2556125 / 21125. Let me compute. 21125 × 100 = 2112500. 2556125 - 2112500 = 443625. 21125 × 20 = 422500. 443625 - 422500 = 21125. 21125 × 1 = 21125. So 21125 × 121 = 2556125. So 2556125/21125 = 121.\n\nSo XD/DY = sqrt(121 · 121/28561) = sqrt(121²/28561) = 121/169.\n\n28561 = 169². So XD/DY = 121/169 = (11/13)².\n\nSo XD/DY = 121/169.\n\nLet me double-check: 2556125/28561 · 121/21125 = (2556125 · 121)/(28561 · 21125) = (2556125/21125) · (121/28561) = 121 · 121/28561 = 14641/28561. sqrt = 121/169.\n\nSo XD/DY = 121/169.\n\nNote 121/169 = (11/13)². And 11 = CA - BC? No. 13 = AB. 11... Let me see: sides are 13, 14, 15. 11 = ? Hmm, 15-4=11, or related to the altitude. Actually 11 doesn't obviously relate. But 121/169 is the answer.\n\nLet me verify the computation once more carefully, especially the key cancellation 2556125/21125 = 121.\n\n21125 × 121: 21125 × 100 = 2112500, 21125 × 20 = 422500, 21125 × 1 = 21125. Total = 2112500 + 422500 + 21125 = 2556125. ✓\n\nAnd 28561 = 169². ✓ (169² = 28561, since 170² = 28900, 169² = 28900 - 340 + 1 = 28561.)\n\nSo XD/DY = 121/169.\n\nThe answer is 121/169.\n\nLet me also sanity check the distances numerically.\nX ≈ (-389/338, 1764/169) ≈ (-1.151, 10.438)\nD = (-0.5, 1)\nY ≈ (209/22, -84/11) ≈ (9.5, -7.636)\n\n|DX| ≈ sqrt((0.651)² + (9.438)²) ≈ sqrt(0.424 + 89.08) ≈ sqrt(89.5) ≈ 9.46\n|DY| ≈ sqrt((10)² + (8.636)²) ≈ sqrt(100 + 74.58) ≈ sqrt(174.58) ≈ 13.21\nRatio ≈ 9.46/13.21 ≈ 0.716. 121/169 ≈ 0.7159. ✓\n\nSo the answer is 121/169.\n\nNow let me write up the proof cleanly.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1787247601}
